<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Terentii Shtykov</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1907–1964</span> · Also known as Terenty Shtykov</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Terentii Shtykov (1907–1964) was a Soviet colonel general and party official who directed the Soviet occupation of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a> from 1945. As the senior political officer of the occupying forces he supervised the Soviet Civil Administration, the rise of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kim-il-sung">Kim Il Sung</a> and the building of a communist state. He became the first Soviet ambassador to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-korea">North Korea</a> in 1948 and was involved in the preparations for the invasion of the South in 1950.</p></div>
